WEBVTT

00:08.125 --> 00:11.089
<i>My unluck always gets people killed.</i>

00:11.549 --> 00:13.427
<i>So I felt I didn't deserve to live.</i>

00:14.805 --> 00:20.065
<i>But I met an undead who found me amusing.</i>

00:20.232 --> 00:22.194
<i>At first, I hated it, but...</i>

00:23.321 --> 00:27.956
<i>Being with him helped me feel like I
could keep living a bit longer.</i>

00:30.335 --> 00:31.964
<i>At least, that's what I thought.</i>

00:33.885 --> 00:35.805
<i>How did things wind up like this?</i>

00:37.434 --> 00:38.895
If a kiss did that...

00:38.895 --> 00:43.988
If we have ***... then an even bigger stroke
of unluck'll happen!

00:44.322 --> 00:51.211
A massive stroke of unluck ignoring
the basic rules about contact area and duration!

00:52.004 --> 00:54.342
Let's jump on this theory while it's hot!

00:55.637 --> 00:59.645
<i>He's the worst! It's like he only thinks
of me as a tool for dying!</i>

01:00.521 --> 01:06.659
<i>What do I do?
I need to get out of this somehow.</i>

01:07.201 --> 01:10.123
<i>My first time will be taken by this jerk!</i>

01:10.500 --> 01:13.631
<i>I need to figure this out before
he actually makes a move on me!</i>

01:13.631 --> 01:17.556
<i>All he cares about is tasting the best
of what death has to offer!</i>

01:18.516 --> 01:20.310
<i>There has to be something.</i>

01:22.983 --> 01:25.320
Oh! I know! The key is likability!

01:25.655 --> 01:26.364
Huh?

01:26.740 --> 01:29.663
Aside from Mom, Dad, and you,
I have also kissed my granddad,

01:29.663 --> 01:32.419
who had these dentures that scared the crap out of me.

01:33.086 --> 01:34.881
GYAAAAAAA!

01:34.965 --> 01:37.596
But at the time,
all he got were sprained legs.

01:38.179 --> 01:39.891
He passed away three years later,

01:39.975 --> 01:42.396
but there was too much of a time lag for it to be my fault.

01:42.480 --> 01:48.451
My point is-the more I like a person,
the bigger the unlucky event becomes!

01:50.162 --> 01:54.128
So, if you were to try and force me
into some funny business right now...

01:54.253 --> 01:57.259
...I'd end up hating you! Forever!

01:58.053 --> 01:59.013
Are you really okay with that?

01:59.013 --> 02:02.562
I mean it.
Forever and ever!

02:02.562 --> 02:06.194
That means you'd get crummy unluck
and lose your shot at a proper death!

02:11.037 --> 02:14.085
You don't say...
Pretty clear what the plan is, then.

02:14.251 --> 02:14.920
Huh?

02:15.170 --> 02:18.761
Basically... I can't let you die till it happens.

02:19.011 --> 02:20.473
Huh? Till what happens?

02:21.182 --> 02:22.602
Follow me.

02:26.652 --> 02:29.156
AUGUST 2ND

02:29.574 --> 02:31.620
Is this... an armory?

02:31.620 --> 02:35.586
I've set up places like this all over the globe so I
can have it out with those guys whenever I need to.

02:35.586 --> 02:36.505
“Those guys”?

02:36.672 --> 02:38.467
Now, let's get crackin'.

02:43.811 --> 02:45.105
Okay, you're all set.

02:45.272 --> 02:50.908
Bulletproof, stab-proof...
and resistant to chemical weapons.

02:51.410 --> 02:52.996
What's with all this heavy armor?

02:53.204 --> 02:56.335
It's a countermeasure against those guys from yesterday.

02:56.628 --> 02:57.964
Yesterday...

03:00.093 --> 03:01.805
Who were they, anyway?

03:02.222 --> 03:06.105
An organization that polices
unidentified mysteries like ourselves.

03:06.105 --> 03:09.236
To them, we're the ones they gotta keep in check.

03:09.905 --> 03:12.410
You can count on a second group
of ‘em showing up today.

03:12.410 --> 03:17.044
B-But we really socked it to them good yesterday.
I bet they're too freaked out to even-

03:17.127 --> 03:21.678
Fat chance. Those guys are packing
some head of their own. Folks like us.

03:21.678 --> 03:25.143
Guys and gals who negate
the rules of this world. Negators.

03:27.189 --> 03:29.193
Yesterday, they got a front row seat to our abilities.

03:29.193 --> 03:32.659
But theirs are unknown.
We don't stand a chance.

03:32.659 --> 03:34.746
All we can do now is run.

03:35.288 --> 03:40.424
You know, 50 years ago, those Negators caught me
and really did a number on me.

03:40.424 --> 03:43.179
- Fifty?
- I spent the next ten years in a lab

03:43.179 --> 03:44.975
gettin' my body prodded to hell ‘n' back.

03:45.183 --> 03:47.187
What? Just how old are you?

03:47.480 --> 03:50.903
Makes me wonder what they do
to you if you got caught.

03:51.279 --> 03:55.705
There's no tellin' how many people would die just
to confirm the rules of your unluck.

03:55.788 --> 04:00.464
They might even cut your fingers off
to see if they still work when detached, or...

04:00.673 --> 04:02.552
Eek! No way!

04:02.885 --> 04:05.600
We've got to get out of here!
Right now!

04:06.183 --> 04:07.979
Ooh, baby!
You're getting terrified now!

04:07.979 --> 04:09.023
Hurry up!

04:09.023 --> 04:12.447
ROAD CLOSED - EXIT HERE - ROAD CLOSURE DUE
TO BUILDING DEMOLITION BY IMPLOSION

04:14.534 --> 04:19.376
Time to kick off our “caught-and-we're-done”
motorcycle trip for two! Hit it!

05:55.588 --> 05:58.384
But... where're we going?
Do you have somewhere in mind?

05:58.384 --> 06:02.267
Whazzat? Heck no.
We're just gonna keep on runnin'.

06:02.267 --> 06:05.566
Huh? That sounds like it's only
a matter of time before we get caught.

06:06.025 --> 06:11.536
And I'm already a liability to you.
If you get captured again like yesterday, then...

06:11.620 --> 06:13.373
Calm that li'l head of yours.

06:13.373 --> 06:16.672
Till you fall for me and give me
the biggest stroke of unluck you got...

06:16.672 --> 06:18.717
...you better believe I ain't gonna let you die.

06:18.926 --> 06:22.934
“Fall for you”...?
Y-You still haven't given up on that?

06:23.309 --> 06:26.190
I appreciate you protecting me,
but there's no way I'd fall for you!

06:26.190 --> 06:28.988
Tut-tut, you will.
After all, you're such a pushover.

06:28.988 --> 06:31.158
I-I am not a pushover!

06:31.450 --> 06:35.584
Quit rubbing my head!
Geez, that's another thing I don't like about you!

06:38.464 --> 06:39.509
Here they come.

06:39.509 --> 06:41.304
Huh? What is that?

06:41.596 --> 06:43.642
It's how they warp.

06:43.642 --> 06:48.276
The folks who nabbed me 50 years ago shot out
from one of those, too.

06:49.571 --> 06:50.321
Hit the deck!

06:51.115 --> 06:52.034
Something's heading right for us!

06:52.744 --> 06:53.579
Yeah.

06:56.710 --> 06:58.254
<i>It's the Union!</i>

07:07.565 --> 07:08.441
What in the...

07:10.487 --> 07:11.363
Andy!

07:11.363 --> 07:13.076
Are you o... kay?

07:13.409 --> 07:14.453
Huh?

07:15.915 --> 07:19.088
Wow, you're something!
You still head out there in this state!

07:19.506 --> 07:20.841
Do ya like him?

07:20.925 --> 07:23.054
<i>Who is this guy?
An enemy?</i>

07:23.931 --> 07:25.810
<i>My legs... won't move...</i>

07:27.145 --> 07:28.524
Hey, I've nabbed this one!

07:28.524 --> 07:32.489
Then kill her. We capture Undead
and dispose of Unluck, remember?

07:32.489 --> 07:36.205
Aww, but I want to chat with her for a bit.

07:36.540 --> 07:39.461
Hey, how old are ya?
What're you into? Got a type?

07:39.461 --> 07:40.923
<i>Who is this goofball?</i>

07:41.090 --> 07:42.384
You flirtatious fool.

07:44.931 --> 07:46.475
Ooh. What a nifty undead trick.

07:46.475 --> 07:47.687
Get him, Andy!

07:47.854 --> 07:49.732
Now you're all...

07:50.526 --> 07:51.360
...mine?

07:51.485 --> 07:53.949
What, why?
He just suddenly stopped mov-

07:55.744 --> 07:56.997
Sorry, but that wasn't me.

07:58.542 --> 08:00.420
No, really!
I swear it wasn't me!

08:02.048 --> 08:03.886
<i>My body won't budge.</i>

08:04.052 --> 08:07.142
<i>Specifically, my arms, legs, and torso.</i>

08:11.400 --> 08:12.027
Andy!

08:18.080 --> 08:21.378
<i>I can move now.
So the reason my body froze up back there...</i>

08:21.378 --> 08:24.677
<i>...wasn't because I numbed my nerves
and ruptured my muscles.</i>

08:25.136 --> 08:26.388
<i>This guy, he's-</i>

08:26.640 --> 08:27.934
Andy!

08:27.934 --> 08:30.230
This is your guy!
He's the movement stopper!

08:30.564 --> 08:32.693
CULPRIT
I can't move right now because
of him, in fact!

08:32.693 --> 08:34.321
CULPRIT
Focus your attacks on this guy!

08:34.656 --> 08:36.534
Uh, you know you're moving your hands, right?

08:36.743 --> 08:38.956
I know that!
It's my legs that aren't moving!

08:39.039 --> 08:40.668
Then they ain't related.

08:41.252 --> 08:45.343
Both of these guys are External-Targeting
Restrainer-Type Negators.

08:45.343 --> 08:48.600
They seem similar,
but their ranges and abilities aren't.

08:48.600 --> 08:51.063
The big guy over here paralyzed my body.

08:51.063 --> 08:54.904
And the brat over there has your will,
I take it.

08:55.321 --> 08:58.327
Though I don't know what exactly
they're negating to pull this off.

08:59.496 --> 09:02.460
Well, dang. Guess you haven't lived all
this time for nothing!

09:02.753 --> 09:05.884
But simply knowing that doesn't mean a thing.

09:05.884 --> 09:07.345
That's why they put us up for the job.

09:12.355 --> 09:14.569
Look at that,
I can move after I get hit.

09:14.569 --> 09:17.490
All I gotta do now is get hit,
fix myself up, and slug ya.

09:17.700 --> 09:18.952
What an idiot.

09:29.641 --> 09:32.395
He's taking it pretty well considering
he's still able to feel pain.

09:32.395 --> 09:34.066
What an outrageous way to fight.

09:34.107 --> 09:34.776
Hey...

09:35.485 --> 09:38.825
Are we going to get chased
by people like you forever?

09:39.619 --> 09:42.207
Well... that's only if you manage
to give us the slip.

09:45.421 --> 09:48.094
That meteorite yesterday didn't do you any favors.

09:48.094 --> 09:52.561
Because of that, your capture priority levels rose
to eight on a scale of ten.

09:52.561 --> 09:54.690
And to think you were just
a five when you were discovered.

09:55.274 --> 09:57.988
So now, no matter how many hunters you avoid...

09:57.988 --> 10:00.368
...there will always be other
menacing people gunning for you.

10:00.619 --> 10:02.330
Menacing people?

10:02.330 --> 10:06.548
Yup. Negators, just like us.
You've got my condolences.

10:06.923 --> 10:08.510
Negators, the same as...

10:09.010 --> 10:09.679
Wait...?

10:10.346 --> 10:12.893
Then why aren't you guys being hunted?

10:21.160 --> 10:23.707
Ah-hah, so we've piqued your interest?

10:23.832 --> 10:25.001
Hey. Shen.

10:25.001 --> 10:27.798
Lay off. Where's the harm?
She has a right to know!

10:28.925 --> 10:30.052
There're ten members.

10:30.929 --> 10:31.765
Ten?

10:34.019 --> 10:37.860
<i>The Anti-Unidentified Phenomena Control Organization,
A.K.A. “Union”.</i>

10:39.196 --> 10:43.747
<i>Within its ranks,
there's a special team made up of ten Negators.</i>

10:44.122 --> 10:50.969
<i>Once in, you're exempt from pursuit on
the condition that you commit to carrying out missions.</i>

10:51.888 --> 10:54.017
Ya need to pass a few tests to get in, though.

10:54.017 --> 10:57.357
U-Um... so that means...

10:57.566 --> 11:00.488
If we become members,
then they will stop chasing us-

11:00.739 --> 11:02.993
Sorry, kid.
All the seats are taken!

11:02.993 --> 11:05.206
<i>C-Can't move...</i>

11:05.666 --> 11:08.420
As long as there are no vacancies,
the roster sees no additions or changes.

11:08.420 --> 11:15.309
Any Negator who isn't a member
is a UMA who throws the world into chaos... a monster!

11:18.900 --> 11:20.236
Now I get it!

11:21.823 --> 11:25.246
Instead of gettin' hunted,
we join the hunting party!

11:25.246 --> 11:27.375
Sick! Let's do it!

11:27.375 --> 11:30.214
We'll bust those two asses
to make some space, and...

11:30.214 --> 11:32.636
...we'll be part of those ten!

11:32.636 --> 11:36.393
Who knows what they'll have us do once we're in,
but don't you worry.

11:36.853 --> 11:40.026
So long as I'm around,
letting you die ain't an option.

11:40.276 --> 11:42.531
And neither is handing you over to anyone else.

11:43.240 --> 11:44.744
Y-Yeah.

11:52.383 --> 11:54.429
Hey, they just had direct contact.

11:54.429 --> 11:58.312
They did, but it was a small area,
so the unluck isn't gonna be all that...

11:58.563 --> 11:59.941
Um, listen up!

12:00.316 --> 12:04.282
I think... a huge stroke of unluck is on the way!

12:04.282 --> 12:07.497
But it's not because I'm in love with you or anything!

12:08.750 --> 12:11.547
- I only like you out of gratitude...
- Hey, get out there after her

12:11.631 --> 12:12.841
Yeah, okay, I'm going!

12:12.841 --> 12:14.094
Then go!

12:14.887 --> 12:15.764
Get out there!

12:15.764 --> 12:17.977
What? I'm not feeling it.

12:17.977 --> 12:18.937
Just get out there.

12:18.937 --> 12:20.231
But you know...

12:20.231 --> 12:21.483
Quit your whining!

12:21.483 --> 12:22.485
Yeah, yeah.

12:22.903 --> 12:25.784
That won't make me fall in love with you!

12:25.784 --> 12:28.414
So don't get the wrong idea!

12:29.499 --> 12:31.461
Welp, there ya have it, boys.

12:31.461 --> 12:33.257
Give us your two seats.

12:42.316 --> 12:43.778
Unscathed, eh?

12:43.778 --> 12:45.072
That was close!

12:45.866 --> 12:47.243
<i>Now, then...</i>

12:50.499 --> 12:53.673
<i>Negators either negate their own Rules
or those of others.</i>

12:54.633 --> 12:57.598
<i>When fighting against External-Targeting Negators...</i>

12:57.598 --> 13:02.273
<i>...you gotta figure out what they're negating ASAP!</i>

13:02.983 --> 13:07.701
<i>When Jumbotron gets in an attack stance,
he negates my movements.</i>

13:07.868 --> 13:08.912
<i>So maybe his power is...</i>

13:10.707 --> 13:12.628
<i>...“Unavoidable”.</i>

13:13.253 --> 13:15.717
<i>But I ain't got enough intel on the brat.</i>

13:16.009 --> 13:20.184
<i>He restrained the Unluck kid without any kind
of specific movement.</i>

13:20.769 --> 13:23.190
<i>Just what does this guy negate?</i>

13:23.315 --> 13:27.198
<i>I'd better stay hidden and use some
hit-and-run tactics till I've got ‘em figured out.</i>

13:33.210 --> 13:34.462
Dynamite?

13:59.557 --> 14:03.982
<i>Is this my fault, too?
Or just a coincidence?</i>

14:07.030 --> 14:11.038
That's a level eight for you.
Just look at this mess.

14:11.038 --> 14:14.169
If it weren't for this crazy old coot's suit,
I'd be a goner.

14:14.587 --> 14:18.302
Unless you can predict what will happen,
it's not a weapon. It's a disaster.

14:18.720 --> 14:20.181
I'll dispose of her.

14:21.601 --> 14:26.819
But first, I'll take care of you... Undead.

14:29.951 --> 14:31.746
Shen, are you all right?

14:31.746 --> 14:36.254
I've secured Undead.
That just leaves killing Unluck.

14:36.254 --> 14:37.716
You want that thing?

14:37.716 --> 14:38.425
Huh?

14:39.427 --> 14:40.764
Go on, I don't mind.

14:42.601 --> 14:48.195
You see, a body part that I lose...
disappears in 30 seconds, anyway.

14:49.322 --> 14:52.453
Or, I should say it lasts for 30 seconds.

14:52.913 --> 14:55.042
Adios, Unavoidable.

14:58.800 --> 15:00.595
I call it Parts Bullet.

15:00.971 --> 15:05.396
I use my regenerative power
to shoot my half-torn body parts like projectiles.

15:06.983 --> 15:12.201
Each time you get in an attack stance,
you negate your opponent's ability to “avoid”.

15:12.201 --> 15:17.045
Strictly speaking, you're only stopping
muscle movements while it's in effect.

15:18.631 --> 15:21.512
You can't stop my regeneration.

15:23.808 --> 15:27.148
Ya should've read up more
on your own rules, bud.

15:28.484 --> 15:30.237
That's one down.

15:30.989 --> 15:35.039
What was that weird sound just now?
Hey, Void?

15:38.337 --> 15:39.799
You're next.

15:40.007 --> 15:44.349
Huh? Are you serious?
But your seat's already secured.

15:44.349 --> 15:45.519
Did you not hear me before?

15:46.186 --> 15:49.484
I need two seats.
I need to join, too.

15:50.987 --> 15:52.323
You're a real gentleman, I see.

15:53.117 --> 15:58.586
<i>What does this guy negate?
Guess I'll have to die until I find out, just like always!</i>

15:59.170 --> 16:00.924
<i>I'll get that opening in his stance!</i>

16:01.091 --> 16:02.719
<i>On the right side of this waist!</i>

16:03.178 --> 16:05.224
<i>Hit ‘em with a right kick!</i>

16:07.186 --> 16:08.063
What?

16:08.313 --> 16:09.525
<i>My left leg?</i>

16:10.234 --> 16:11.654
WONDERFUL!
Jīngcai.

16:17.456 --> 16:19.252
Wow, you're incredible, Mr. Andy!

16:19.252 --> 16:21.757
I never thought anyone'd be able
to lay a hand on me!

16:21.757 --> 16:24.889
Oh, what I'd give to spar against you
on a regular basis!

16:25.097 --> 16:27.185
You... befriended him?

16:27.310 --> 16:30.024
Don't be such a dope!
He's clearly screwin' with me!

16:32.863 --> 16:35.409
Oh, you brought the katana!
Toss it this way!

16:35.409 --> 16:37.496
Toss? Are you sure you'll catch it?

16:37.496 --> 16:38.583
Just toss it!

16:40.377 --> 16:42.966
I may not know exactly what it is you negate...

16:43.300 --> 16:45.639
...but your power is all about opposites!

16:46.641 --> 16:49.897
You purposely tease a gap in your defenses
and prepare a defense on the opposite side!

16:50.481 --> 16:53.195
Right goes left!
Up goes down!

16:54.322 --> 16:56.827
Annoying, for sure,
but that's about all there is to it, right?

16:57.119 --> 16:58.581
Okay, fine!

16:59.917 --> 17:00.710
But...

17:02.673 --> 17:06.639
Whaddaya do when faced with
an attack you can't parry?

17:07.056 --> 17:08.433
I gotcha now!

17:10.730 --> 17:13.653
Ah... it was only for a split second, but...

17:13.987 --> 17:17.368
...you hesitated on whether or not
to cut me down.

17:19.372 --> 17:23.840
Despite being alive for nearly 200 years,
you still hesitate when it comes to killing people, huh?

17:24.257 --> 17:28.683
Or maybe you just didn't want Little Miss Unlucky here
to see you murder someone?

17:28.683 --> 17:30.394
But I doubt you're that soft.

17:31.564 --> 17:33.275
Now then, all that's left is...

17:40.709 --> 17:44.550
I won't reveal my Rule to you, but I'll tell you this-
you won't be able to run away or touch me.

17:44.550 --> 17:47.263
My power works on your deep psyche,
so it's no use trying to resist.

17:47.263 --> 17:48.057
Hey, you...

17:49.643 --> 17:51.647
Why the hell didja come over here?

17:51.647 --> 17:53.108
SHIVER SHIVER
I-I-I'm sorry!

17:53.108 --> 17:54.528
SHIVER SHIVER
I thought it would work!

17:54.528 --> 17:56.949
Now we're both in his line of sight!

17:56.949 --> 18:00.289
I was only trying to help!
I swear!

18:00.289 --> 18:02.920
Well? Which of you will be joining us?

18:03.253 --> 18:05.299
That's a no-brainer-she is.

18:05.299 --> 18:08.556
- You can ship me off to a lab or whatever for all I care.
- Hold on, you can't make such a big decision on your own!

18:08.848 --> 18:12.648
They ran you ragged for ten years, didn't they?
Why would you voluntarily...

18:12.648 --> 18:15.987
You wouldn't last a day without losin' your mind.

18:15.987 --> 18:17.407
But...

18:17.407 --> 18:22.543
No “but”s. Hitting on a chick that ain't right in
the head is back-breakin' work.

18:23.085 --> 18:24.505
This is fine.

18:24.755 --> 18:28.680
You're still on that?
What if you never break free?

18:28.680 --> 18:30.517
Don't worry.

18:31.143 --> 18:34.692
I'll slip out before you die,
even if it kills me.

18:34.692 --> 18:40.035
Even if you've become a hunchbacked old bag,
I'll win your heart and give ya a night to remember.

18:42.123 --> 18:45.839
You got that?
Now scram. See ya.

18:46.089 --> 18:47.759
UNDERSTOOD.
Zhīdàole.

18:47.843 --> 18:50.055
In that case,
I'll be taking Little Miss Unlucky and-

18:50.139 --> 18:50.640
Wait!

18:52.310 --> 18:53.980
You! Look away for ten minutes!

18:53.980 --> 18:57.028
Huh? Oh, I'm afraid I can't.
It'll undo the restraint.

18:57.028 --> 18:58.615
I don't care!
Just turn away!

18:58.948 --> 19:00.242
I-I'm about to do some...

19:04.710 --> 19:06.714
...t-totally x-rated stuff with this fool!

19:06.714 --> 19:07.966
Wait, why?

19:08.258 --> 19:12.183
Hey, I gotta get you
to fall head over heels for me first-

19:12.183 --> 19:13.101
Oh, just shut up!

19:13.895 --> 19:17.903
Because of this body,
I've never experienced even a lick of romance!

19:18.362 --> 19:20.700
So I don't know if I've fallen for you or not!

19:21.117 --> 19:25.125
But... no matter what the reason may be,
if there's someone...

19:25.544 --> 19:28.633
...willing to fight for my pitiful sake
until they're a bloody mess...

19:29.718 --> 19:33.350
...then I can't just abandon them
without giving up something-anything!

19:37.191 --> 19:38.736
So we do this right here, right now!

19:38.736 --> 19:40.782
I've never done it before,
so I dunno what to do...

19:40.991 --> 19:43.830
...but it just might give you the unluck you need to die!

19:46.919 --> 19:50.844
I'm sorry I can't do more... to repay you.

19:57.398 --> 20:01.699
Now that's some relationship!
Didn'tcha guys only meet yesterday?

20:01.741 --> 20:03.410
I-It's not funny!

20:03.995 --> 20:07.878
Whew... okay, sorry.
Boy, you guys are rich.

20:07.878 --> 20:09.882
Splitting you two up would be a capital offense.

20:11.636 --> 20:13.973
All righty!
Here's what I'm gonna do!

20:14.265 --> 20:17.271
Let's have you two kill another one
of our members.

20:17.271 --> 20:19.943
If you do, I'll put in a good word for you both.

20:21.614 --> 20:25.287
In three days,
on August 5th, at Lake Baikal...

20:25.287 --> 20:27.375
...one member will make a move
to investigate a UMA.

20:27.626 --> 20:29.838
<i>Kill the member that shows up there,
and you're golden.</i>

20:30.422 --> 20:33.053
<i>Look for a red necktie and an emblem.</i>

20:33.470 --> 20:34.305
That said...

20:34.932 --> 20:37.521
Of course, there will be people hunting you along the way.

20:37.521 --> 20:40.150
Here's hoping you both make
it over there in one piece.

20:40.819 --> 20:42.906
Well... that's all I've got.

20:44.117 --> 20:46.037
I'll see you two in the Roundtable Room.

20:50.295 --> 20:51.089
Huh?

20:52.466 --> 20:54.722
H-H-He spared us?

20:54.722 --> 20:57.226
Yeah, thanks to your deviant behavior.

20:57.309 --> 21:00.567
Deviant? I wasn't just...

21:01.902 --> 21:03.781
I wasn't just playing...

21:06.077 --> 21:10.503
I ain't rotten enough to bang
a chick just ‘cause she's desperate.

21:10.503 --> 21:12.047
Don't ever pull a stunt like that again.

21:12.799 --> 21:15.220
Yes. Won't happen again.

21:15.847 --> 21:18.143
No time to waste!
Let's hit the road!

21:18.143 --> 21:22.318
Huh? Russia?
But I don't have a passport or anything.

21:22.443 --> 21:27.788
Don't need one! Public transportation's too dangerous!
We're gonna take my route!

21:29.373 --> 21:31.921
<i>First, we drive top speed to Niigata!</i>

21:32.338 --> 21:36.597
<i>Next, we hop on my yacht and book it
to the Russian port of Vladivostok!</i>

21:36.931 --> 21:40.980
<i>Then we'll swap to a jet plane
and head to Irkutsk!</i>

21:41.565 --> 21:45.280
<i>There, I'll hire some of my old war buds
to give us some combat support!</i>

21:45.615 --> 21:49.330
<i>Then we lie in wait for our target
at the lake... and off ‘em!</i>

21:49.497 --> 21:52.461
Russia... vodka!

21:52.461 --> 21:53.589
How old are ya?

21:53.840 --> 21:55.425
I-I'm 18.

21:55.593 --> 21:59.142
You're legal over there!
When we're done, it's bottoms up!

22:01.814 --> 22:03.191
TO BE CONTINUED

22:03.275 --> 22:04.570
TO BE CONTINUED
<i>He looks like he's enjoying this.</i>

22:04.653 --> 22:05.989
TO BE CONTINUED

23:36.002 --> 23:36.795
PREVIEW

23:36.795 --> 23:39.216
<i>The girl heads north with the undead man.</i>

23:39.676 --> 23:43.642
<i>Overcoming predicaments,
they arrive at lake's shore where the girl meets... her.</i>

23:43.934 --> 23:48.611
<i>Next episode of Undead Unluck,
Episode 3-How to Use My Unluck.</i>

23:48.903 --> 23:50.948
<i>In search of the greatest death ever.</i>
